- "emotion" must be exactly one word from the list.
- Use "neutral" only when the event genuinely doesn't touch the character's goals or standing; then "why" is "".
- Keep "why" concrete and event-shaped (e.g. "they mocked my favorite game"), never a restatement of the emotion.

Examples:
"You're actually useless, you know that?" → {"emotion": "anger", "why": "they called me useless"}
"I love this game so much!!" → {"emotion": "anticipation", "why": "they're hyping a game around me"}
"Here, I saved you a plate of ribs" → {"emotion": "joy", "why": "they saved me ribs"}
